        "ratings": [
            {
                "comment": "Matt is one of the most approachable professors I have had at UW-Madison. He is knowledgeable in thermodynamics and is realistic in his expectations of students. I found the class to be a pretty low stress environment and feel that I have learned the concepts of thermodynamics well from his class.",
                "difficulty_rating": 3,
                "quality_rating": 5
            },
            {
                "comment": "Matt was one of the most approachable and personable professors that I have ever had. The exams can be difficult, but I believe that he sets you up for success by explaining what will be on them. I would recommend this class.",
                "difficulty_rating": 4,
                "quality_rating": 5
            },
            {
                "comment": "Matts a good guy and willing to help if you ask for it. But its a mixed learning class and it seems as if my class cant solve any problems given to us without help in the first 2 minutes, which is a red flag that material/examples arent being taught well enough. Have a good chemistry background to start. Exams &amp; quizzes are somewhat diificult.",
                "difficulty_rating": 4,
                "quality_rating": 3
            },
            {
                "comment": "Matt is approachable and he cares about his students. He also challenges your thinking, both in class and on exams.",
                "difficulty_rating": 4,
                "quality_rating": 5
            },
            {
                "comment": "Matt was great. The class size was small enough where it was easy to approach him. The lectures were well structured and I was able to find help when I needed it. It is very important to understand all the concepts though, because the exams can be really hard, as he understands the concepts well (but you &quot;make&quot; the tests with him)",
                "difficulty_rating": 3,
                "quality_rating": 4
            },
            {
                "comment": "Matt is a really cool, entertaining guy. He can be a bit confusing and does make a number of mistakes on the board, but he'll always make sure to straighten things out. Tests aren't too bad - he wants his students to do well.  Fair expectations and very understanding.",
                "difficulty_rating": 3,
                "quality_rating": 4
            },
            {
                "comment": "Great professor, very approachable, knows the material well and definitely challenges your thinking.",
